Task: classifier-tests + classifier-impl (plan agui_hitl_interrupts_a1f3c2d8, phase P1)

Why: spec FR2. The processor needs a reason before it can build an
input_required interrupt, and hosts need a hook because the yes/no vs
form distinction is a UI judgement the launcher cannot always make.

Changes:
- agui/internal/interrupt/classify.go (new): ReasonClassifier type,
  ClassifyReason (host classifier first, empty falls through),
  ReasonForSchema and isBooleanShaped (the default shape rule).
- agui/internal/interrupt/classify_test.go (new): 9 shape cases plus 5
  ClassifyReason cases covering nil classifier, custom reason wins,
  empty falls through, and the classifier receiving the request.
- agui/agui.go: AGUIConfig.interruptReasonClassifier field and the
  WithInterruptReasonClassifier option.
- agui/interrupt_classifier_test.go (new): option stores the classifier;
  zero config leaves it nil.

Design notes:
- ClassifyReason takes the already-converted responseSchema map rather
  than re-deriving it from req.ResponseSchema, because the caller needs
  the same map to build the interrupt and SchemaToMap logs on failure.
- The option signature takes a plain func rather than an exported alias
  of interrupt.ReasonClassifier, since that type lives in an internal
  package external callers cannot name.
- isBooleanShaped extracts the single property without a loop-and-return,
  which removed an unreachable trailing return and took the function to
  100% coverage.
- A property schema may legally be a bare JSON 'true'; that is not an
  object and does not pin the property to a boolean, so it stays
  input_required.

Coverage: all new functions 100%; interrupt package 71.8% -> 75.5%.
Verification: go fmt, go vet, CI=true go test ./... all clean.
